{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "extrapolate_linear_ghost",
    "description": "Pointwise one-cell halo value outside a domain wall from the two innermost cells a (the wall cell) and b (its inward neighbour): the linear extrapolation 2 a - b, guarded from below by max(2 a - b, a, b) -- fire_behavior's Extrapol_var_at_bdys with BIAS = 1 ((1 - BIAS)(2a - b) + BIAS max(2a - b, a, b)). For a level-set (signed-distance) field increasing toward the wall (a > b, the fire inside the domain) the guard is inactive and the ghost is the pure linear extrapolation; when the field decreases toward the wall the ghost is clamped to the larger of the two inner values, so the one-sided difference across the wall is never steeper than the field's own slope and never changes sign spuriously. Exact on a linear field with a >= b. Match-less helper bound by every *_extrapolate_bc rule of this grid (the bc:extrapolate_linear closure).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:bc",
      "axes:x",
      "order:2",
      "stencil_width:2"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls, Select_eno, Select_weno5, Select_4th, Select_godunov (case 4), Extrapol_var_at_bdys. The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [],
  "expression_templates": {
    "extrapolate_linear_ghost": {
      "params": [
        "a",
        "b"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "max",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  2,
                  "a"
                ]
              },
              "b"
            ]
          },
          "a",
          "b"
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
